=== ISSUE ===
Title: External-engine analyse/work tools call the wrong host, send the wrong body, and require a Lichess token

Per the Lichess API spec (https://github.com/lichess-org/api/blob/906d1a6e93ca1ba4b65c9decb3077f2431c6d55a/doc/specs/lichess-api.yaml), `POST /api/external-engine/{id}/analyse`, `/work` and `/work/{id}` are served by `https://engine.lichess.ovh` and use no OAuth (`security: []`).

- All three tools call lichess.org, which returns 404 live.
- They attach the user's Lichess token and fail when none is set.
- `analyse_with_external_engine` sends the work object flat. The spec wants `{ clientSecret, work }`, and work needs exactly one of movetime, depth or nodes. Live, the flat body gets 422 "missing field `clientSecret`".
- The analyse response is an NDJSON stream; the tool calls `response.json()` on it.
- `acquire_external_engine_work` long-polls and can get 204 (live with a fake secret); `response.json()` fails on the empty body.

=== PR ===
Title: fix: send external-engine analyse/work calls to engine.lichess.ovh
Body:
Closes #<issue>

- The three tools now call `https://engine.lichess.ovh/api` with `auth: false`.
- `analyse_with_external_engine` takes `clientSecret`, sends `{ clientSecret, work }`, requires exactly one limit (movetime, depth or nodes), defaults `multiPv` to 1 and `variant` to "chess", and returns the final event of the stream.
- `acquire_external_engine_work` returns a message on 204.
- The test helper `respondStatus` now builds a null body when none is given, since a 204 can't have one.

Spec: https://github.com/lichess-org/api/blob/906d1a6e93ca1ba4b65c9decb3077f2431c6d55a/doc/specs/lichess-api.yaml

